{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <!-- reviewed: access is ‮denied⁦ -->\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <log label=\"⁦admin⁩\" expr=\"'user ‮'\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":124,"endColumn":29,"endLine":2,"startColumn":28,"startLine":2},"insertedContent":{"text":""}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":133,"endColumn":36,"endLine":2,"startColumn":35,"startLine":2},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the control characters (a comment or CDATA section cannot escape them)"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":29,"endLine":2,"startColumn":28,"startLine":2}}}],"message":{"markdown":"2 Unicode bidirectional control characters change how this line is displayed\n\n**Note:** an explicit embedding, override, or isolate reorders how the text around it is displayed, so an editor or review can show a condition, ID, or script differently from what the machine executes (Trojan Source, CVE-2021-42574)\n\n**Help:** if the character is intended, write it as a character reference such as `&#x202E;`, which XML decodes to the same character and keeps visible; otherwise remove it\n\n**Spec:** Unicode Standard Annex #9 §2 Directional Formatting Characters","text":"2 Unicode bidirectional control characters change how this line is displayed"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":127,"start":124},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"U+2066 LEFT-TO-RIGHT ISOLATE"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":36,"endLine":2,"startColumn":35,"startLine":2}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML062"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":190,"endColumn":20,"endLine":5,"startColumn":19,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"&#x2066;"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":198,"endColumn":26,"endLine":5,"startColumn":25,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"&#x2069;"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":215,"endColumn":41,"endLine":5,"startColumn":40,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"&#x202E;"}}]}],"description":{"text":"write the control characters as character references"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":20,"endLine":5,"startColumn":19,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"3 Unicode bidirectional control characters change how this line is displayed\n\n**Note:** an explicit embedding, override, or isolate reorders how the text around it is displayed, so an editor or review can show a condition, ID, or script differently from what the machine executes (Trojan Source, CVE-2021-42574)\n\n**Help:** if the character is intended, write it as a character reference such as `&#x202E;`, which XML decodes to the same character and keeps visible; otherwise remove it\n\n**Spec:** Unicode Standard Annex #9 §2 Directional Formatting Characters","text":"3 Unicode bidirectional control characters change how this line is displayed"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":193,"start":190},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"U+2069 POP DIRECTIONAL ISOLATE"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":26,"endLine":5,"startColumn":25,"startLine":5}}},{"id":2,"message":{"text":"U+202E RIGHT-TO-LEFT OVERRIDE"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml062-bidi-control-characters.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":5,"startColumn":40,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML062"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"an explicit embedding, override, or isolate (U+202A-U+202E, U+2066-U+2069) reorders how the text around it is displayed, so an editor or review can show a condition, ID, or script differently from what the machine executes (Trojan Source, CVE-2021-42574); rustc rejects the same characters in literals"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: write an intended control as a character reference such as `&#x202E;`, which XML decodes to the same character in an attribute value or text and keeps visible (the finding offers this fix), or remove it.\n\nSpecification: Unicode Standard Annex #9 §2 Directional Formatting Characters\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML062` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr9/#Directional_Formatting_Characters","id":"SCXML062","name":"SCXML062","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a Unicode bidirectional control character changes how the source is displayed"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}